      "body": "## Summary\n\nDecision record for #5808: the postcard wire schema v1 — envelope byte layout, discriminator assignments, flag semantics, size limits, and normative golden vectors.\n\nDecided against the named parent draft (#5674 issue body, §1–§2, checked fresh 2026-11-16), following the sibling precedent: #5809 (versioning) and #5810 (framing) were decided and merged the same way while the parent record is still pending, and #5810 explicitly leaves the final byte layout and the `fragmented` flag semantics to #5808. Parent precedence is stated in the record: if the final #5674 record conflicts, the parent wins and this record is revised.\n\n## What it settles\n\n- Envelope: fixed field order (major, minor, discriminator, flags, sender, optional recipient, stream, sequence, timestamp, extensions/TLV, payload), postcard v1 encodings throughout, ratifying the live `pkgs/id` practice (id-sync meta protocol `/iroh-meta/3`: append-only discriminants pinned by test, exact decode rejecting trailing bytes, 1 MiB cap).\n- Discriminators 0–6 for the parent §1 message family, append-only, with the error kind's code table fixed so the oldest peer can always report a mismatch (#5809 invariant 6).\n- Flags: compressed / encrypted / fragmented — `fragmented` is a provenance marker for #5810 checked-chunk reassembly, never a decoder instruction.\n- Four golden vectors (42/76/80/43 bytes) plus negative vectors, each verified to decode field-for-field against the record's own layout.\n- One named deviation from the parent draft, recorded in the open in D1/§7: no separate in-envelope payload-length field — the payload's postcard length prefix and the carrier framing already carry it, and a third copy could disagree with both.\n\n## Scope\n\nDocs only — no code, no change to any live protocol. `Closes #5808` on merge per the issue's acceptance (close a design with a recorded decision in a `doc/` record).\n\nQueue task 12892, lane code-b.\n\nCloses #5808\n",
