      "body": "Closes the design half of #5811 (parent #5674 decomposition item 4). Design only — no implementation.\n\n## What this settles\n\nThe browser/restrictive-network adapter is **one adapter with two carrier modes over the same ID session**:\n\n1. **WSS (primary)** — a *stream* carrier in #5810's framing class. It carries the existing length-prefixed frames (`pkgs/id/src/frames.rs`, 1 MiB cap) unmodified, one ID frame per WebSocket binary message, reusing the transport-neutral `SessionIo` seam already proven by `pkgs/id/src/web/world_ws.rs`.\n2. **HTTPS request/response (fallback)** — POST batches plus a long-poll or SSE response stream, in #5810's chunked carrier class. Same frames, request-scoped transport envelope, no new protocol.\n\nThe fallback degrades **timing only**, never semantics or identity: no live retry, no live queue, no reordering, session resume by session ID + sequence, and TLS is never ID identity.\n\n## Cost of the fallback (as the issue asks)\n\n- **Latency:** +1 RTT per client→server batch, plus poll interval server→client. Acceptable for durable and low-rate live traffic; **not** acceptable for high-rate live input — the layer above must be able to reduce or refuse it rather than silently carry it.\n- **Semantics:** no offline queue, checkpoint thresholds unchanged (256 frames / 2 s / commit), gaps detectable but not filled.\n- **Resources:** browsers cap connections per origin (~6 on HTTP/1.1), so HTTPS mode must multiplex onto few connections — a reason to prefer SSE over many long-polls.\n\n## Not re-decided\n\nNo #5674, #2036 or #5791 decision changes. Candidate ordering, probing, memory, overrides and failure classification stay with #5791 (`doc/2026-11-05T13-38-00Z_design_id5791_transport_negotiation.md`). Messaging semantics stay with #2036.\n\n## Written against named drafts\n\n#5808, #5809, #5810, #5813 and #5815 are all still open, so §6 states the explicit interface this adapter needs from each, and §7 states the ten invariants implementation must hold.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Doc only; no code, build or test changes. Every `file:line` citation re-checked against `origin/main` at `0a27a7f19f`.\n- `doc/` has no prior adapter record for #5811 (confirmed by search at this baseline).\n\nCloses #5811\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796723271&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7613&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7613&signature=e3cae91e6e2a34451bf49729e0bb42e69efcb49f69489e29a2312c0f817671f7\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7613?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
