      "body": "Partial decision record for #5814 (queue task 13680, lane code-l).\n\nAdds `doc/2026-11-08T23-22-53Z_design_id_adapter-conformance/` and indexes it in `doc/README.md`.\n\nDecided now:\n- One shared contract harness in pkgs/id (generalising the shell_contract / world_session contract-test patterns); adapters enter through assertion-free bindings; both directions and both pairings checked.\n- Certification criteria C1–C6 pinned to the four load-bearing elements of #5975 (wire format, identity, capability negotiation, registry format) plus carrier honesty and a no-waivers rule.\n- Interop matrix axes: adapter × carrier class × platform, with pairing (reference peer + cross-adapter) and direction as in-cell dimensions.\n- CI gate: the suite as a pkgs/id flake check in the existing `id` workflow PR gate; the full matrix nightly, with nightly failure revoking a cell's certified status.\n- Fixture/oracle model: canonical wire scripts with per-step declared outcome classes — a pass is machine-decidable. Rejected alternatives recorded: per-adapter bespoke tests, manual certification, snapshot/golden-file-only oracles, self-peer-only testing.\n\nBlocked remainder (§7): per-sibling fixture content and matrix rows fill in as #5808/#5809/#5810/#5811/#5812/#5813 land (all verified OPEN 2026-11-08). Per the record, #5814 stays open for that remainder — this PR deliberately carries no closing keyword, in the decided-now/blocked-remainder shape of the #5866 record.\n\nNo #5674 or #5975 decision is changed (§8 states the one near boundary explicitly: the merge gate binds this repo's adapter PRs, not anyone else's conformance).\n\nTests (doc-only): every relative link in the new record resolves (checked programmatically — none broken), the doc/README.md index link target exists, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n",
