      },
      "body": "Review-gated PoC for issue #2261 (follow-up B of #2050), opened by queue task 5810 (lane code-a). What is here: the scheduling policy that did not exist - pkgs/id/crates/id-core/src/swarm.rs, a pure deterministic scheduler the get fetch loop can drive. Rarest-first disjoint chunk-group assignment across at most 4 holders (hand-fed provider list, as #2261 permits while #2260 is open; consumes HeldRanges from id-core holders.rs). Verified group completes with per-range provenance logged; bad group discards, requeues, deprioritises the holder; missing-range close shrinks that holders known ranges and requeues elsewhere; endgame duplicate-requests trailing in-flight ranges (first verified wins); nobody-home surfaces as a distinct uncovered-range signal, never a generic failure; optimistic unknown-ranges mode supported. Tests: 7 new tests named for their oracles (disjointness/coverage, source cap, requeue+deprioritise, missing-shrink, nobody-home, endgame, optimistic); full id-core lib suite 454 passed, 0 failed. What is NOT here yet (recorded on #2261): wiring the scheduler into the live get fetch loop over iroh-blobs range requests, the zero-local-copy fetch demo from 2+ live holders, and the network benchmark table (1 vs 2 vs 4 holders, partial mix, holder-leaves, observe-off). Per the #2050 program rule this PoC does not merge as the permanent feature without the review round.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797413162&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=10660&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F10660&signature=d0c29e3e3ea58100ef0212af6a27ef0db8b94c4392a7966e240a7b6a3a43aa10\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https:/