      "body": "Design decision record for #5812 (from parent #5674), following the sibling pattern of #5811's WSS/HTTPS adapter record. Design only — no code changed.\n\nDecisions recorded in `doc/2026-11-14T13-10-00Z_design_id5812_adapter_record.md`:\n- **One adapter contract** for all carriers: postcard frames carried unchanged (#5810 length-prefixed framing, 1 MiB cap), declared class mapping (durable/chained vs ephemeral/live), ID-layer identity always authoritative (carrier authentication — TLS, DTLS, OS credentials — is transport evidence only, per #5674's hard rule and #2036's transport-is-not-authority), capability-gated dialling per #5809, failures classified in #5791's vocabulary.\n- **WebRTC**: per-class data channels (reliable/ordered for durable, unreliable/unordered for ephemeral with loss surfaced), signalling carried as #2036 control frames over any working path (no hosted signalling service), TURN as a dumb pipe. Placed inside #5791's relay-assisted tier — recorded explicitly as an interface obligation to #5791, not a silent fork; no parent decision changes.\n- **TCP/TLS**: the #5791 TCP tier — one TLS 1.3 connection per peer session, both classes on the one stream, session layer enforces no-backlog semantics.\n- **Local IPC**: Unix socket / named pipe with the identical framing; OS peer credentials as a pre-filter only, ID handshake still authoritative; the programme's one recorded exemption from transport TLS, bounded to same-machine.\n\nRejected alternatives are recorded per adapter (hosted signalling, reliable-only WebRTC, WebSocket framing for the TCP tier, per-class connections, plaintext upgrade, shared-memory IPC, skipping the ID handshake on IPC, localhost TCP as the local transport). Six implementation invariants; implementation timing remains a separate decision per the issue.\n\nCloses #5812 on merge.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797253590&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=9996&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F9996&signature=d05ed492cb15d6097f0ea2768f550bd3f3447a78fbe05bd8e6d9ff072dad7e0b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/9996?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
